{"findings":[{"category":"install","severity":"high","summary":"fmt.pc is generated but never packaged into an install target","evidence":"CMake installs fmt.pc to ${FMT_PKGCONFIG_DIR} (lib/pkgconfig). Bazel has a write_file rule gen_fmt_pc that produces fmt.pc, but there is no pkg_files target that includes it — consumers of the install tree get no pkgconfig file.","cmake_ref":"CMakeLists.txt:442"},{"category":"install","severity":"high","summary":"Compiled fmt library binary absent from install layout","evidence":"CMake installs the fmt archive/shared object to ${FMT_LIB_DIR} (lib/) via install(TARGETS fmt fmt-header-only … LIBRARY DESTINATION … ARCHIVE DESTINATION …). The only Bazel install target is install_files__include_fmt, which only covers headers; the library binary has no pkg_files counterpart.","cmake_ref":"CMakeLists.txt:423"},{"category":"install","severity":"medium","summary":"CMake package config and version files not generated or installed","evidence":"CMake generates fmt-config.cmake, fmt-config-version.cmake (write_basic_package_version_file), and fmt-targets.cmake (install EXPORT), then installs them to ${FMT_CMAKE_DIR} (lib/cmake/fmt). FMT_INSTALL=ON is baked in but Bazel has no rules_pkg or genrule producing these files, so downstream CMake find_package(fmt) from the Bazel install tree would fail.","cmake_ref":"CMakeLists.txt:436"},{"category":"test","severity":"medium","summary":"std-test missing filesystem library detection and conditional link","evidence":"CMake uses try_compile to detect which library (if any) provides std::filesystem (e.g. -lstdc++fs on GCC 8/9) and calls target_link_libraries(std-test ${STDLIBFS}). The Bazel std-test has no linkopts for the filesystem library; tests using std::filesystem on GCC 8/9 would fail to link.","cmake_ref":"test/CMakeLists.txt:96"},{"category":"flag","severity":"medium","summary":"scan-test unconditionally defines FMT_HAVE_STRPTIME without symbol-existence check","evidence":"CMake runs check_symbol_exists(strptime \"time.h\" HAVE_STRPTIME) and only defines FMT_HAVE_STRPTIME if the symbol is found. Bazel unconditionally sets local_defines = [\"FMT_HAVE_STRPTIME\"] (BUILD line 1122), silently enabling strptime code paths on targets where strptime may not exist (e.g. MSVC).","cmake_ref":"test/CMakeLists.txt:90"},{"category":"flag","severity":"low","summary":"fmt and fmt-header-only do not enforce C++11 minimum standard on consumers","evidence":"CMake calls target_compile_features(fmt PUBLIC cxx_std_11) and target_compile_features(fmt-header-only INTERFACE cxx_std_11), propagating the C++11 requirement to all downstream targets. Neither the fmt nor fmt-header-only cc_library in Bazel sets a features or toolchains constraint, so a consumer compiling with C++98 would get cryptic template errors rather than a clean standard-version diagnostic.","cmake_ref":"CMakeLists.txt:316"},{"category":"target","severity":"low","summary":"gtest not linked against thread library","evidence":"test/gtest/CMakeLists.txt calls find_package(Threads) and target_link_libraries(gtest ${CMAKE_THREAD_LIBS_INIT}), or defines GTEST_HAS_PTHREAD=0 if threads are absent. The Bazel gtest cc_library has no linkopts for pthreads and no GTEST_HAS_PTHREAD=0 fallback, which can cause linker warnings or failures on platforms where gtest requires explicit pthread linking.","cmake_ref":"test/gtest/CMakeLists.txt:14"}]}
